<h1 class="center">ABSTRACT</h1>
<br>
<p>Public transit systems and regional bus depots face severe operational friction when managing fleet schedules, tracking en-route assets, and resolving service irregularities such as "bus bunching"—where consecutive buses on the same route cluster together, creating service delays and passenger overcrowding. This project presents the <strong>Bus Tracking and Management Application</strong>, an enterprise depot management software engineered in modern C++ utilizing object-oriented programming (OOP) paradigms. The software addresses depot-level dispatching and monitoring through a unified, high-efficiency operational workflow.</p>
<p>Office staff and depot administrators can register fleet buses (registration number, model, capacity) and allocate vehicles to daily routes with driver ID, conductor ID, and departure timings while enforcing schedule uniqueness and fleet availability. The system provides immediate visibility into all registered rolling stock and active route assignments. Crucially, the depot manager can enter or update sample real-time bus locations and execute the autonomous <strong>Same-Route Bus Proximity Engine</strong>. Utilizing the spherical Haversine distance algorithm, the engine performs pairwise spatial analysis across all co-routed buses. Whenever two or more buses on the same route approach within a critical threshold (e.g., &le; 0.75 km), the system triggers high-visibility alerts with actionable headway regulation advisories.</p>
<p>Built on robust OOP principles—including abstract base classes, inheritance, runtime polymorphism via virtual functions, encapsulation, operator overloading, templates, custom exception hierarchies, and CSV file persistence—the application eliminates scheduling collisions and provides actionable situational awareness. Comprehensive testing validates fault-tolerant operation, accurate proximity detection, and rapid telemetry responsiveness.</p>
<br>
<p><strong>Keywords:</strong> C++; Object-Oriented Programming; Intelligent Transportation Systems; Bus Depot Management; Vehicle Tracking; Spatial Proximity Algorithm; Bus Bunching Detection.</p>

