<h2>4.3 Algorithms Used</h2>

<h3>Algorithm 1: Haversine Great-Circle Spatial Distance Metric</h3>
<p>Calculates spherical distance between coordinates (&phi;<sub>1</sub>, &lambda;<sub>1</sub>) and (&phi;<sub>2</sub>, &lambda;<sub>2</sub>):</p>
<ol>
    <li>&Delta;&phi; = (&phi;<sub>2</sub> - &phi;<sub>1</sub>) &times; &pi;/180, &Delta;&lambda; = (&lambda;<sub>2</sub> - &lambda;<sub>1</sub>) &times; &pi;/180</li>
    <li><i>a</i> = sin<sup>2</sup>(&Delta;&phi;/2) + cos(&phi;<sub>1</sub>&times;&pi;/180) &times; cos(&phi;<sub>2</sub>&times;&pi;/180) &times; sin<sup>2</sup>(&Delta;&lambda;/2)</li>
    <li><i>c</i> = 2 &times; atan2(&radic;<i>a</i>, &radic;(1 - <i>a</i>))</li>
    <li><i>d</i> = <i>R</i> &times; <i>c</i>, where <i>R</i> = 6371.0 km.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Complexity:</strong> Time: <i>O(1)</i>, Space: <i>O(1)</i>.</p>

<h3>Algorithm 2: Same-Route Bus Proximity &amp; Bunching Detection</h3>
<ol>
    <li>Group all active bus assignments by their <code>routeId</code> into an associative map: <code>routeId &rarr; vector&lt;busReg&gt;</code>.</li>
    <li>For each route containing 2 or more buses:</li>
    <li>Iterate through all unique pairs (<i>i</i>, <i>j</i>) where <i>i &lt; j</i>.</li>
    <li>Compute ground distance: <i>dist</i> = <code>b1.getCurrentLocation().distanceTo(b2.getCurrentLocation())</code>.</li>
    <li>If <i>dist &le; 0.75 km</i>: trigger <strong>CRITICAL PROXIMITY CONFLICT ALERT</strong> with corrective speed advisory.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Complexity:</strong> Time: <i>O(K &times; N<sub>r</sub><sup>2</sup>)</i>, Space: <i>O(N)</i>.</p>

<h2>4.4 Data Structures Used</h2>
<p class="caption">Table 5: Data structures and their purpose</p>
<table>
    <tr>
        <th>Data structure</th>
        <th>Where used</th>
        <th>Why chosen</th>
        <th>Complexity of key operations</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><code>std::map&lt;std::string, Bus&gt;</code></td>
        <td>Fleet Directory</td>
        <td>Fast ordered lookup by bus registration number.</td>
        <td>Lookup: <i>O(log N)</i>, Insert: <i>O(log N)</i></td>
    </tr>
