<h1>CHAPTER 6: IMPLEMENTATION</h1>

<h2>6.1 Mapping of OOP Concepts to the Code</h2>
<p class="caption">Table 9: OOP concepts and where they are used</p>
<table>
    <tr>
        <th>OOP concept</th>
        <th>Class / file where used</th>
        <th>How it is used and why</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Classes and objects</td>
        <td><code>Bus</code>, <code>Route</code>, <code>Stop</code>, <code>RouteAssignment</code></td>
        <td>Encapsulates physical fleet entities, timetables, and waypoints.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Encapsulation / data hiding</td>
        <td>All classes</td>
        <td>State variables are private; access is controlled via public getters/setters.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Abstraction</td>
        <td><code>Vehicle</code> class</td>
        <td>Abstract base class with pure virtual function <code>virtual void displayDetails() const = 0</code>.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Inheritance</td>
        <td><code>Bus</code> : public <code>Vehicle</code></td>
        <td>Derived concrete class inherits registration, model, and capacity attributes.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Compile-time polymorphism</td>
        <td><code>Bus</code> class (<code>operator&lt;&lt;</code>)</td>
        <td>Stream insertion operator overloading for formatted bus output.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Run-time polymorphism</td>
        <td><code>Vehicle</code> virtual destructor and virtual methods</td>
        <td>Enables dynamic polymorphic dispatch through base class pointers.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Constructors &amp; Destructors</td>
        <td>All classes</td>
        <td>Default/parameterized constructors initialize state; <code>virtual ~Vehicle() = default</code> ensures safe deletion.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Static members</td>
        <td><code>Bus</code>, <code>RouteAssignment</code>, <code>BusDepotApplication</code></td>
        <td><code>totalBusesRegistered</code>, <code>totalAssignments</code>, and <code>proximityAlertEvents</code> track global totals.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Friend functions</td>
        <td><code>printAssignmentRow</code>, <code>operator&lt;&lt;</code></td>
        <td>Allows non-member formatting functions direct access to private fields.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Templates</td>
        <td><code>printHeader&lt;T&gt;</code></td>
        <td>Generic templated header banner printer.</td>
    </tr>
</table>

